  "title": "Enlightenment of the Buddha at Bodh Gaya",
  "summary": "According to Buddhist tradition, Siddhartha sat beneath a holy tree near Uruvela in Magadha, now Bodh Gaya, vowed to stay until he understood how to live without suffering, and became the Buddha. The year is traditional and debated; one account dates the start of his teaching to 527 BC.",
